# Embedded code

Each fence below names a language with a native printer, so its contents are formatted as that language.

```ts
const value: number = 1;
function add(a: number, b: number) {
  return a + b;
}
```

```tsx
const element = (
  <div className="a">{value}</div>
);
```

```js
let list = [1, 2, 3].map((x) => x * 2);
```

```json
{
  "a": 1,
  "b": [true, false, null],
  "c": { "d": "e" }
}
```

```css
a {
  color: red;
  background: blue;
}
.b > .c {
  margin: 0 auto;
}
```

```scss
$color: red;
.a {
  .b {
    color: $color;
  }
}
```

```yaml
key:   value
list:
    * one
    *   two
```

```graphql
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    name
    friends {
      name
    }
  }
}
```

A fence with no language is left as written:

```
const   untouched = 1
```

A fence with an unknown language is left too:

```not-a-language
whatever   goes
```

- a fence inside a list item:

  ```json
  { "inside": "a list" }
  ```

> ```css
> a {
>   color: red;
> }
> ```

